From c6c6d2f90d589970452ebb000534f6bb4905ac64 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Ford <ryan@ryanford.ca>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 17:47:02 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 39/46] rift_s: resync camera frame time after a clock
 discontinuity

IMU samples are ignored until the first SLAM frame is accepted, so the
first frame's epoch offset is computed against an IMU timestamp of 0.
When the extended IMU clock is a 2^32 us epoch ahead of the camera
clock, that frame maps to a negative monotonic time and is rejected as
"went backward". last_frame_time then stays 0, IMU stays ignored, the
epoch offset is never corrected, and every following frame is rejected
too: no head tracking, an empty grey Room View in Room Setup.

Seen on 8 of 8 starts on one headset, e.g.:
  frame_ts=1625067443000 imu_ts=0 hw2mono=-3395444712931
  -> mono=-1770377269931 (now=2524604154978)
with the IMU clock at 5920 s vs the camera at 1625 s once IMU ran.

Treat a backward step of more than a second as a discontinuity and
accept the frame. It is not fresh, so it is not submitted to SLAM, but
it ungates IMU; the next frame gets the correct epoch offset and maps
to ~now.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit e9a098e31308dbf04ca913f653b7cd4a33c286d6)
---
 src/xrt/drivers/rift_s/rift_s_tracker.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/xrt/drivers/rift_s/rift_s_tracker.c b/src/xrt/drivers/rift_s/rift_s_tracker.c
index 6ac51bb..89a8798 100644
--- a/src/xrt/drivers/rift_s/rift_s_tracker.c
+++ b/src/xrt/drivers/rift_s/rift_s_tracker.c
@@ -869,7 +869,15 @@ rift_s_tracker_push_slam_frames(struct rift_s_tracker *t,
 
 
 	timepoint_ns frame_mono_ns = raw_frame_ts_to_mono_ts(t, frame_ts_ns);
-	if (frame_mono_ns < t->last_frame_time) {
+	if (t->last_frame_time - frame_mono_ns > (timepoint_ns)U_TIME_1S_IN_NS) {
+		/* A clock discontinuity, not jitter. At startup IMU samples are ignored until the
+		 * first frame is accepted, so the first frame's epoch offset is computed without
+		 * IMU time; when the IMU clock is a 2^32 us epoch ahead that frame maps far into
+		 * the past (or before 0). Rejecting it would keep last_frame_time at 0, keep IMU
+		 * ignored and the epoch uncorrected, so every later frame would be rejected too. */
+		RIFT_S_WARN("Camera clock discontinuity of %" PRId64 " ns; resyncing frame time",
+		            frame_mono_ns - t->last_frame_time);
+	} else if (frame_mono_ns < t->last_frame_time) {
 		RIFT_S_WARN("Camera frame time went backward by %" PRId64 " ns", frame_mono_ns - t->last_frame_time);
 		os_mutex_unlock(&t->mutex);
 		return;
-- 
